---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { resolve } from 'node:path';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const release = JSON.parse(readFileSync(resolve(process.cwd(), 'public/release/v1/release.json'), 'utf8'));
---

<Base title="Static release status · World Emergency & Hotlines" description="Statically provable World Hotlines build and release information; not live monitoring.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">Static build evidence</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-semibold text-fg sm:text-5xl">Status</h1>
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-elev p-5">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg">What this build proves</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">At build time, the generated release descriptor loaded successfully and indexed <strong>{release.artifact_index.artifact_count}</strong> integration artifacts under release <code class="break-all">{release.release_id}</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-amber-400/60 bg-amber-400/10 p-5">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg">This is not live monitoring</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">This static page does not test the website, CDN, API paths, widget, providers, phone numbers, or network reachability after deployment. It does not report hotline availability, operating status, incidents, uptime, response time, eligibility, or successful contact.</p>
    </div>
    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-fg">Technical-health reference contract</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">A static, synthetic <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/technical-health/v1/README.md">privacy-safe technical-health contract</a> defines a thresholded weekly aggregate and deterministic local dashboard document. This build does not collect those metrics. Metric absence or suppression is not shown as success, health, uptime, or availability.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">A separate <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/assurance-packs/v1/README.md">static synthetic assurance-pack v1 contract</a> demonstrates bounded release/dataset pinning, evidence-review summaries, uncertainty, and replacement disclosure. It is not a live assurance service, customer/provider export, paid offer, or claim about availability or quality; provider claims remain untrusted pending or rejected input.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">The <a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/provider-claims/v1/README.md">static synthetic provider-claim v1 contract</a> demonstrates staging and conflict-free independent review only. It is not a provider portal or live intake/review service; acceptance means candidate eligibility for a separate approved workflow, never canonical publication, verification, or ranking.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-fg">Inspect the evidence</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm"><a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/release">Release and verification guide</a><a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/release/v1/release.json">Machine-readable descriptor</a><a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/release/v1/artifacts.json">Checksum index</a><a class="text-accent hover:underline" href="/releases">Release changelog</a></div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-fg-muted">All public integration surfaces remain static beta with no uptime, support, or SLA commitment. If an artifact cannot be fetched or verified, integrators should use their reviewed degraded behavior and revalidate before promotion.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
